e as a mathematician, astronomer, chemist, geodesist, surveyor, cartographer, metrologist, engineer, and inventor. He was a psychologist, a philologist, a lexicographer, a historian of science, a lifelong student of medicine, and, above all, a philosopher, whose special fields were logic and semiotics. He is widely credited with being the founder of pragmatism. In terms of his importance as a philosopher and a scientist, he has been compared to Plato and Aristotle. He himself intended \"to make a philosophy like that of Aristotle.\" Peirce was also a tormented and in many ways tragic figure. He suffered throughout his life from various ailments, including a painful facial neuralgia, and had wide swings of mood which frequently left him depressed to the state of inertia, and other times found him explosively violent. Despite his consistent belief that ideas could find meaning only if they \"worked\" in the world, he himself found it almost impossible to make satisfactory economic and social arrangements for himself.","publicationYear":1993,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Philosophers","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-charles-sanders-peirce-a-life-joseph-brent"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"United States","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-charles-sanders-peirce-a-life-joseph-brent"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Peirce, Charles S. (Charles Sanders), 1839-1914","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-charles-sanders-peirce-a-life-joseph-brent"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Biography","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-charles-sanders-peirce-a-life-joseph-brent"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Indiana, biography","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-charles-sanders-peirce-a-life-joseph-brent"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","la